[38;5;252m[1m## Two real mismatches found and fixed[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Both were in the output layer, not the arithmetic. The arithmetic and [38;5;10mscanf[0m emulation in the existing translation were already correct, including the awkward parts ([38;5;10mstrtol[0m saturating at [38;5;10mlong[0m then truncating to the low 32 bits, so [38;5;10m4294967296[0m and [38;5;10m-9223372036854775808[0m both reach [38;5;10mbad()[0m).[0m[0m
[0m[0m
1. [38;5;10mprintln![0m panics when a write fails. With stdout on [38;5;10m/dev/full[0m the C exited 0 silently; the Rust aborted with status 134 and a panic message on stderr. [38;5;10mprintf[0m reports failure only via its return value, which the C ignores. Output now goes through a buffer written once with [38;5;10mwrite_all[0m, discarding write and flush errors — which also reproduces glibc's block-buffered single-[38;5;10mwrite[0m-at-exit pattern.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
2. The Rust runtime sets [38;5;10mSIGPIPE[0m to [38;5;10mSIG_IGN[0m before [38;5;10mmain[0m. Into a closed pipe the C died from signal 13 (status 141) while the Rust did not. [38;5;10mmain[0m now restores [38;5;10mSIG_DFL[0m first thing.[0m[0m
